 "cues_why": {
  "shrug": "silent: the shrug is a picture gag, the narration lands it",
  "flash": "silent: the camera_shutter at the same moment is the sound of the flash",
  "sip": "silent: mouth sounds under the narrator's voice read badly",
  "blink, twitch": "a tiny pop, 25 dB under the voice: felt more than heard",
  "freeze": "the pause is a button press (a soft click) and the music's stop (the cue sheet's silence); a synthesised tape-stop read as an explosion or a door",
  "stamp": "the red NO stamp (No interview, No contract ...) is the rubber stamp over a low thump; a YES stamp (p.kind yes, or spoken on \"yes\") is stamp_yes",
  "story_levels": "Story effects (the stamps, the cry, the sneeze, the phone ringing, the ka-ching and the credit alert, the gavel, the coins, the swoon, the stings, the clang) sit about 12-15 dB under the voice as heard, loud enough for phone speakers; pops, whooshes, card lands and UI ticks stay 20 dB or more under (build_mix.py reports both).",
  "baby_cry": "the newborn (Q01) and the new baby (Q03): a brief soft cry, two windows alternating, in the pause after the word",
  "sneeze": "\"You sneeze once\" and \"the same sneeze\": one small sneeze, the same both times (that is the joke)",
  "gavel": "Mum's wooden spoon as a gavel: tok-tok on \"Judgment already passed\", and again for the United Nations; a cue with p.kind 'one' is a single tap",
  "meter": "\"First name. Middle name. Surname.\": one low pizzicato note per name, climbing E-flat, G, B-flat",
  "stings": "sting_1 (deadpan, falling) on \"the fourth one is also doctor\"; sting_2 (cheeky, rising) after \"Not if. When.\"",
  "crunch": "silent: mouth sounds under the narrator read badly"
 },
